WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.986
No one ever said married life would be easy, but Meg did not expect it to be so challenging.

2
00:00:05.987 --> 00:00:12.493
John was a kind, loving husband who helped Meg in every way possible, for which she was truly grateful.

3
00:00:12.494 --> 00:00:19.510
Still, Meg found the little chores in everyday life that she had taken for granted at home were now a huge challenge for her.

4
00:00:19.510 --> 00:00:26.607
Then of course there were new issues that Meg had never experienced at home but had to learn to deal with as a married woman.

5
00:00:26.607 --> 00:00:33.190
One day, as she was doing the simple act of preparing a meal, Meg felt dizzy and sick to her stomach.

6
00:00:33.190 --> 00:00:38.359
Fortunately, John was in the kitchen at the time and carried her to the sofa.

7
00:00:38.359 --> 00:00:43.993
"Can I bring you anything? Water? A blanket?" he asked in a concerned voice.

8
00:00:43.994 --> 00:00:47.741
"Just some hot tea, thank you," Meg said faintly.

9
00:00:47.742 --> 00:00:51.580
By the time John brought the drink to her, Meg had gotten worse.

10
00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:55.719
"Darling, I feel very ill," she told her husband.

11
00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:59.834
"Shall I fetch Dr. Bangs?" he asked, squeezing her hand tightly.

12
00:00:59.835 --> 00:01:03.660
"No," Meg said. "I need my mother."

13
00:01:03.661 --> 00:01:08.375
John raced out of the house and down the street to get his mother-in-law, who, along with Beth,

14
00:01:08.376 --> 00:01:13.586
was in the process of giving each window in the house a good shine before the winter set in.

15
00:01:13.587 --> 00:01:18.605
"John! What's the matter?" Mother asked him when she saw his worried look.

16
00:01:18.605 --> 00:01:24.774
"It's Meg," he said, gasping for breath. "She's not well and I don't know what to do."

17
00:01:24.775 --> 00:01:31.575
Throwing down her cloth, Mother wiped her hands and said, "Let's not waste another moment while the poor girl lies sick."

18
00:01:31.576 --> 00:01:36.644
When they got to Meg and John's house, Meg was sweating and looking very pale.

19
00:01:36.644 --> 00:01:43.363
Mother put her hand on Meg's forehead, over her heart, then down on her stomach. Then, surprisingly, Mother smiled.

20
00:01:43.363 --> 00:01:48.923
"What's the matter with her?" John asked, his voice trembling. "Is Meg going to be all right?"

21
00:01:48.924 --> 00:01:56.028
"She's going to be fine," Mother replied, nodding. "Meg isn't sick—she's pregnant."

22
00:01:56.029 --> 00:02:02.541
Upon hearing those words, John collapsed into a heap on the floor next to his wife.

23
00:02:02.542 --> 00:02:07.663
Meanwhile, Jo, who was not yet aware that she was soon going to become an aunt,

24
00:02:07.664 --> 00:02:13.388
spent her days content to be a governess and her evenings very happy to be with a friend.

25
00:02:13.389 --> 00:02:20.304
"Jo, this week you must try to read this thrilling adventure that will take you across the seas,"

26
00:02:20.305 --> 00:02:25.073
the Professor said, handing Jo a thick, old book from his own collection.

27
00:02:25.074 --> 00:02:31.488
Since their first encounter a couple of weeks ago, Jo found that she had a lot in common with the Professor.

28
00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:37.974
They both loved to read and write, though she preferred writing fictional stories and he favored poetry.

29
00:02:37.975 --> 00:02:43.326
When he had moved to America, the Professor was forced to leave behind many of his possessions

30
00:02:43.327 --> 00:02:50.348
but he could not bear to part with his beloved collection of books, which he now displayed proudly in his personal library.

31
00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:56.005
Jo considered it an honor that the Professor wanted her to read some of his dearest treasures

32
00:02:56.006 --> 00:03:02.085
(though at first when he offered her his favorite book, she did not have the heart to tell him that she could not read German).

33
00:03:02.086 --> 00:03:09.619
Fortunately, the Professor owned a series of books translated into English that Jo was able to enjoy thoroughly.

34
00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:14.508
On the weekends, the Professor would invite Jo to go with him and his nephews to the park

35
00:03:14.509 --> 00:03:20.913
or to take a carriage to Coney Island, an amusement park where children (of all ages) could go on rides.

36
00:03:20.914 --> 00:03:26.310
Jo noticed that the more time she spent with the Professor, the broader her horizon became.

37
00:03:26.311 --> 00:03:29.935
There seemed to be no end to the amount of knowledge to be learned.

38
00:03:29.936 --> 00:03:37.555
Because the Professor was teaching her so many new things, Jo wanted to show her thanks but she couldn't find a way to do so.

39
00:03:37.556 --> 00:03:42.470
Then one evening, the opportunity arose as she was washing her clothes.

40
00:03:42.471 --> 00:03:49.695
She happened to find two pairs of his socks, which he had probably dropped without realizing, on the floor of the laundry room.

41
00:03:49.695 --> 00:03:55.972
They were still damp and as Jo laid them out to dry, she noticed they all had holes in them.

42
00:03:55.973 --> 00:03:59.481
Smiling to herself as she recalled the first time she met him,

43
00:03:59.482 --> 00:04:06.047
Jo was about to leave when it occurred to her that perhaps she could help the Professor by mending his holey socks.

44
00:04:06.048 --> 00:04:11.452
"I'll bring them back here after I do it so he won't know it was me," Jo thought to herself.

45
00:04:11.452 --> 00:04:17.955
Putting the socks into her laundry basket, she quickly climbed the stairs to her room and took out her sewing kit.

46
00:04:17.956 --> 00:04:25.036
While Meg had just found out she was soon to be a mother and Jo was experiencing feelings she had never felt before,

47
00:04:25.037 --> 00:04:28.746
Amy was also discovering something new about herself.

48
00:04:28.747 --> 00:04:34.810
She sensed that any day now, Fred was going to propose to her and she was prepared.

49
00:04:34.811 --> 00:04:41.268
Sure enough, one chilly evening, Fred made an unannounced visit to Amy and her aunt.

50
00:04:41.269 --> 00:04:48.814
"Why, Fred," Aunt March said fondly, for she was sure that he would be a perfect match for her grandniece.

51
00:04:48.814 --> 00:04:53.649
"What a pleasant surprise! To what do we owe this honor?"

52
00:04:53.650 --> 00:05:01.486
Amy sat quietly clasping her trembling hands while she waited for the now inescapable question to fall from Fred's lips.

53
00:05:01.487 --> 00:05:05.540
As he spoke to Aunt March, revealing his love for Amy, she watched him,

54
00:05:05.541 --> 00:05:11.608
feeling horrible about what she was going to do but at the same time knowing it was the right thing.

55
00:05:11.609 --> 00:05:18.376
Before she knew it, Fred was on bended knee asking, "Amy March, will you be my wife?"

56
00:05:18.377 --> 00:05:23.978
Aunt March relaxed in her chair, absolutely certain what Amy's answer would be.

57
00:05:23.979 --> 00:05:28.829
"I'm sorry, Fred, I can't marry you," Amy said clearly.

58
00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:32.581
"What?" Aunt March's eyes bulged in shock.

59
00:05:32.582 --> 00:05:37.047
"Amy, did you hear what Fred said? He wants to marry you!"

60
00:05:37.048 --> 00:05:42.513
"I know, Aunt March, but I don't want to marry him," Amy said respectfully.

61
00:05:42.514 --> 00:05:45.450
"But why not?" demanded the old woman.

62
00:05:45.451 --> 00:05:50.011
Poor Fred was in a state of such shock that he was speechless.

63
00:05:50.012 --> 00:05:53.583
"Because I don't love him," Amy admitted honestly.

64
00:05:53.584 --> 00:05:59.288
"And I must marry for love or I won't be truly happy. I know that now."

65
00:05:59.289 --> 00:06:06.552
If only Jo could have heard Amy's admission at that moment, she would have marveled at how her sister had changed.

66
00:06:06.553 --> 00:06:14.382
And if Amy, for her part, could have seen Jo secretly smiling as she tenderly placed the mended socks back in the laundry room,

67
00:06:14.383 --> 00:06:18.192
Amy would have been shocked at the difference in her sister as well.

68
00:06:18.193 --> 00:06:24.755
Winter was coming to an end, which meant that this chapter of Jo's journey would conclude shortly too.

69
00:06:24.756 --> 00:06:32.318
Jo's stay in New York had exceeded all her expectations and more as she looked back on her six months away from home.

70
00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:39.824
Feeling stronger, more mature, as well as more fulfilled, Jo readied herself to make the trip home.

71
00:06:39.824 --> 00:06:50.026
At the same time, she felt a dull ache in her heart because that meant she would have to say good-bye to a dear friend.

